.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-AUTOINSTALL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-autoinstall
.Nd install, redeploy or roll back a machine with nobody at it, when the live system is told to
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs at every boot of the kldload live system, from
.Pa kldload-autoinstall.service .
It does nothing unless it is told to, in one of these ways, checked in this
order:
.Bl -enum
.It
a
.Ql kldload.seed= Ns Ar url
on the kernel command line, which the netboot server puts there for a
machine it has armed; the answers are fetched from
.Ar url ;
.It
a seed disk: a FAT volume labelled
.Ql KLDLOADSEED
holding
.Pa answers.env ;
.It
.Pa /etc/kldload/autoinstall.env
built into the image;
.It
answers given one by one on the kernel command line, as
.Ql kldload. Ns Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value ,
which override any of the above.
.El
.Pp
With none of them it logs that there was nothing and exits 0: it is safe to
leave enabled.
A seed URL that does not answer \(em the normal state of a machine nobody
has armed \(em also stops it, with exit 0; it never falls back to another
source, since a machine told to install from one place must not install
something else instead.
.Pp
Then, by
.Ql kldload.action= :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm install
The default.
It fills in what the answers lack \(em the disk, if none is named, and the
secrets \(em and hands them to
.Xr kldload-install-target 8 .
.It Cm deploy
Receive a ZFS archive onto
.Ql kldload.disk=
instead of installing packages: from
.Ql kldload.source= Ns Ar host : Ns Ar dataset
over ssh, or from
.Ql kldload.archive-url=
over HTTP, with
.Xr kldload-restore-machine 8 .
.It Cm rollback
Import the pool and list its boot environments, changing nothing; with
.Ql kldload.be= ,
make that one the pool's
.Cm bootfs .
.El
.Ss Answers from the kernel command line
Each value must match its key's pattern, or nothing is installed:
the answers are read as root just before a disk is wiped.
.Bl -column "k8sbootstrap" "KLDLOAD_ENABLE_SECURE_BOOT" -offset indent -compact
.It Sy key Ta Sy sets
.It distro Ta Ev KLDLOAD_DISTRO
.It profile Ta Ev KLDLOAD_PROFILE
.It hostname Ta Ev KLDLOAD_HOSTNAME
.It disk Ta Ev KLDLOAD_DISK
.It username Ta Ev KLDLOAD_USERNAME
.It timezone Ta Ev KLDLOAD_TIMEZONE
.It locale Ta Ev KLDLOAD_LOCALE
.It keyboard Ta Ev KLDLOAD_KEYBOARD_LAYOUT
.It suite Ta Ev KLDLOAD_SUITE
.It zfs Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ENABLE_ZFS
.It encrypt Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ZFS_ENCRYPT
.It topology Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ZFS_TOPOLOGY
.It secureboot Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ENABLE_SECURE_BOOT
.It buildimages Ta Ev KLDLOAD_BUILD_IMAGES
.It keepnetboot Ta Ev KLDLOAD_KEEP_NETBOOT
.It kvm Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ENABLE_KVM
.It k8s Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ENABLE_K8S
.It k8sbootstrap Ta Ev KLDLOAD_K8S_BOOTSTRAP
.It zfsdev Ta Ev KLDLOAD_KLAB_ZFS_DEV
.It ai Ta Ev KLDLOAD_ENABLE_AI
.It template Ta Ev KLDLOAD_TEMPLATE Pq Ql none No clears it
.El
.Pp
An install must name a distribution.
Any other
.Ql kldload.\&
key is ignored.
.Ss Secrets
Passwords are never taken from the kernel command line, which every user
of the live system can read: a
.Ql kldload.password= ,
.Ql .passphrase= ,
.Ql .rhel_user=
or
.Ql .rhel_pass=
there is named in the log and dropped.
A password the answers do not carry \(em the user's, the disk passphrase
when encryption is on, the Red Hat login for RHEL \(em is asked for on the
machine's own screen: it writes what it needs to
.Pa /run/kldload/install-needs ,
the install screen asks, and it waits up to an hour for
.Pa /run/kldload/install-secrets .
The values are never logged, and the answers file is kept mode 0600.
.Ss Choosing the disk
With no disk named, it looks at every whole disk and describes what is on
it: a partition table, any signature
.Xr blkid 8
knows on the disk or its partitions, and
.Fx
GELI, which
.Xr blkid 8
cannot see and which is read from the disk's last sector.
The live medium and the seed disk are never candidates.
A disk is chosen only if it is the one empty disk; with no empty disk, a
disk holding only kldload's own
.Ql rpool
and its EFI partition is chosen as a reinstall.
More than one empty disk, or none usable, is a refusal.
A disk that cannot be read is not empty.
The disk is written into the answers by its
.Pa /dev/disk/by-id
name.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
For testing; none is set in use.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE
Read this file instead of
.Pa /proc/cmdline .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG
Log here instead of
.Pa /var/log/installer/autoinstall.log .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN
Print the answers assembled from the command line and exit 0, before the
disk is chosen.
It does not stop
.Cm deploy
or
.Cm rollback ,
which run before it.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_STOP_BEFORE_EXEC
Print the final answers and exit 0 where the installer would start.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_RUNDIR
Instead of
.Pa /run/kldload ,
for the secrets exchange.
.It Ev KLDLOAD_SECRETS_TIMEOUT
Seconds to wait for secrets; default 3600.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/log/installer/autoinstall.log
Everything it says.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/autoinstall.env
Answers built into the image.
.It Pa /run/kldload/install-needs , Pa install-secrets
The request for secrets, and the answer.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Nothing to do, the seed URL did not answer, a rollback listing, or a
rollback done; otherwise it does not return, but becomes the installer or
the restore.
.It 1
Refused.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, as a user, with the test
variables and a file standing in for the kernel command line.
Nothing was installed.
.Ss Answers from the command line
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat cmdline
BOOT_IMAGE=vmlinuz rd.live.image kldload.distro=debian kldload.profile=server kldload.hostname=node7 kldload.timezone=America/Denver kldload.kvm=1
$ KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE=cmdline KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG=ai.log KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN=1 kldload-autoinstall
[2026-09-30 01:18:09] [autoinstall] Scanning for KLDLOADSEED disk...
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] Building answers from the kernel cmdline (no seed file present)
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   cmdline: KLDLOAD_DISTRO=debian
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   cmdline: KLDLOAD_PROFILE=server
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   cmdline: KLDLOAD_HOSTNAME=node7
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   cmdline: KLDLOAD_TIMEZONE=America/Denver
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   cmdline: KLDLOAD_ENABLE_KVM=1
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] Applied 5 answer(s) from the kernel cmdline
