KLDLOAD_PROFILE=server
KLDLOAD_HOSTNAME=node7
KLDLOAD_TIMEZONE=America/Denver
KLDLOAD_ENABLE_KVM=1
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss A value that does not fit
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat cmdline
kldload.distro=fedora kldload.hostname=bad;name
$ KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE=cmdline KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG=ai.log KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN=1 kldload-autoinstall
\&...
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] REFUSING: kldload.hostname=bad;name does not match ^[a-zA-Z0-9]([a-zA-Z0-9-]{0,61}[a-zA-Z0-9])?$
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall]   An answers file is read as root just before a disk wipe. NOT installing.
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss A password on the command line
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat cmdline
kldload.distro=fedora kldload.password=hunter2
$ KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE=cmdline KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG=ai.log KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN=1 kldload-autoinstall
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] Scanning for KLDLOADSEED disk...
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] REFUSED kldload.password= from the kernel cmdline: /proc/cmdline is world-readable; it will be asked on screen
\&...
KLDLOAD_DISTRO=fedora
# (exited 0)
.Ed
.Ss Two seeds
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat cmdline
kldload.seed=http://a/x.env kldload.seed=http://b/y.env
$ KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE=cmdline KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG=ai.log KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN=1 kldload-autoinstall
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] REFUSING: 2 kldload.seed= on the kernel cmdline — expected one. NOT installing.
# (exited 1)
.Ed
.Ss A machine that is not armed
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ cat cmdline
kldload.seed=http://127.0.0.1:9/aa-bb-cc-dd-ee-ff.env
$ KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_CMDLINE=cmdline KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_LOG=ai.log KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN=1 kldload-autoinstall
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] Seed URL on cmdline: http://127.0.0.1:9/aa-bb-cc-dd-ee-ff.env
curl: (7) Failed to connect to 127.0.0.1 port 9 after 0 ms: Could not connect to server
# (exited 0)
[2026-09-30 01:18:10] [autoinstall] Seed URL did not answer (not armed, or unreachable) — NOT installing
.Ed
.Pp
The last line arrives after the exit: output goes to the log through
.Xr tee 1 ,
which can finish after the script.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-install-target 8 ,
.Xr kldload-netboot-server 8 ,
.Xr kldload-restore-machine 8
.Sh HISTORY
Its disk choice once looked at five fixed device names and took any disk
without a ZFS signature as empty; on 2026-09-11 a storage server's eight
.Fx
GELI disks, which Linux sees as blank, were the most attractive
targets on the machine.
The seed label it looked for, with a hyphen, is one character too long
for FAT and could not be made (found 2026-09-07).
Until 2026-09-23 passwords on the command line were used, and so were
readable by every user of the live system.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a seed URL that was not http or https
exited 0, like a machine nobody had armed, and the second seed label was
never looked for.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
.Ev KLDLOAD_AUTOINSTALL_DRYRUN
does not make
.Cm deploy
or
.Cm rollback
safe to try: they act before it is looked at.
.Pp
.Cm rollback
with
.Ql kldload.be=
imports the pool forced, past a claim by another system.
